{
  "contract": "inverter-settings-v1",
  "family": "deye_tou",
  "note": "DEYE-022 (docs/28-deye-inverter-control.md sections 4, 5.2 and 5.4): the Deye hybrid control family, shared by the Home Assistant (ha-solarman) and the Deye Cloud path. Roles are catalog keys (inverterSettings.json). intents by IntentKind code: end device = only Time of Use program roles (the inverter ends it at the next program start); end lease = also a global role, restored by the lease holder. A target is {const} (a catalog value), {from} (an input the intent carries: powerW for charge, charge_to_soc and discharge, targetSoc for charge_to_soc, limitW for export_limit; currentSoc and socFloor for any). window: the fields of the program the window takes; otherPrograms: the fields every other program carries while the intent holds. requires: settings the intent reads but never writes. registers: which keys share one register (on Deye each role has its own), with its budget class. Data only: nothing here is written before units 2b, 4 and 5 and the owner switch. touDayValues: the ISO weekdays each touDays value runs on (the rawBit0 catch-all \"enabled\" has none: a value that does not round-trip is never snapshotted). selfUse: the fields of a self-use program slot ({\"owner\": true}: the highest value of that field among the owner's own programs, filled by the Home Assistant component; every slot SOC is at least socFloor, applied by the one program builder). programRequires: settings read before every program write but a restore (a self-use slot under Export First would sell the battery to its floor, docs/28 section 4). floors: the capability each program field may not go below (applied by the one program builder). functionIntents (DEYE-030): intents that are functions of their own, not battery modes (the export limit): never offered as an intent, and a mode's apply never lets go their roles.",
